# Docs-first rule — Mamla.AI

## Step 1 — Always start here (zero codebase reading required)

Open **`docs/00-agent-quickref.md`** first. It is a single page containing:
- Exact file paths for every backend app, view, URL config, and frontend component
- MongoDB collection names
- API URL prefixes
- Auth rules and key conventions
- Environment variables
- Route table

This one file replaces scanning 50+ source files. Read it, find where to go, open only that file.

## Step 2 — Open the relevant detail doc only if you need more depth

| Task | Detail doc |
|------|-----------|
| Backend (Django, APIs, auth, DB, Celery) | `docs/02-backend-legalv1.md` |
| API endpoints and auth requirements | `docs/04-api-reference.md` |
| eCourts scraper/API (court data) | `docs/06-ecourts-scraper.md` |
| Frontend (React, routes, Redux, Axios) | `docs/03-frontend-webpack.md` |
| Architecture overview | `docs/01-architecture-overview.md` |
| What changed / what to do next | `docs/05-changelog-and-improvements.md` |

## Step 3 — Make the change

Use the exact paths from the docs. Do not guess file locations.

## Step 4 — Update the docs (mandatory)

After every change, update the relevant doc(s) in the same commit/response:

| Change made | Update this |
|-------------|------------|
| New or changed API endpoint | `docs/04-api-reference.md` + URL table in `docs/02-backend-legalv1.md` |
| New Django app | `docs/02-backend-legalv1.md` app table + `docs/01-architecture-overview.md` repo layout + `docs/00-agent-quickref.md` prefix table |
| New frontend route or component | `docs/03-frontend-webpack.md` route table + `docs/00-agent-quickref.md` routes table |
| New env var | `docs/02-backend-legalv1.md` env section + `docs/00-agent-quickref.md` env table |
| Auth flow change | `docs/02-backend-legalv1.md` auth section + `docs/03-frontend-webpack.md` auth flow |
| eCourts change | `docs/06-ecourts-scraper.md` |
| Completed feature / bug fix | `docs/05-changelog-and-improvements.md` §2 "What Was Done" table |
| Architecture refactor | `docs/01-architecture-overview.md` + `docs/05-changelog-and-improvements.md` |
| Any path in quickref is wrong | `docs/00-agent-quickref.md` immediately |

## Hard constraints (never violate)

- ❌ Do NOT scan the codebase to find where something lives — use docs/00-agent-quickref.md.
- ❌ Do NOT add a second auth system — Supabase only (`@supabase_required` decorator).
- ❌ Do NOT use Django ORM models — apps use raw MongoDB via `core.init_clients.get_mongo_client()`.
- ❌ Do NOT hardcode `mamla.ai` or `127.0.0.1:8000` — use `FRONTEND_URL` env (backend) and `AxiosInstance` (frontend).
- ❌ Do NOT leave docs stale — update in the same response as the code change.
